WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:08.700
Thanks, Coach Bobby.

2
00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:13.440
All right, team, before we make great pizzas, provide great service, or

3
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:17.400
show off the legendary sense of urgency, we have to look like we're

4
00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:18.240
ready to play.

5
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.400
Your uniform is your game day jersey.

6
00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:25.120
When it's clean, complete, and worn correctly, it tells the

7
00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.980
customer, "I'm prepared, I'm professional, and I take pride in

8
00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:33.000
representing Domino's." Because let's be honest, if you walk

9
00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:36.970
into a restaurant and the employee looks like they just lost a wrestling match with

10
00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:40.060
their laundry basket, you might have some questions.

11
00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:44.020
Perfect image isn't about being a fashion model.

12
00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:48.540
It's about cleanliness, food safety, professionalism, and

13
00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:51.980
giving customers confidence before we make their order.

14
00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:56.860
Let's start at the top of our shirts.

15
00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:01.500
Always wear a Domino's approved uniform or promotional shirt.

16
00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:05.980
Your uniform should be clean, in good condition, and worn

17
00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:06.539
correctly.

18
00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:12.280
Undershirts should follow the approved color guidelines,

19
00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:17.040
have no distracting patterns, and anything hanging below the

20
00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:18.900
uniform shirt should be tucked in.

21
00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:23.880
If you're working with food and wearing long sleeves, roll those sleeves

22
00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:24.840
above the elbow.

23
00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:27.899
Remember, the uniform shirt is the starter.

24
00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:32.220
Everything underneath still has to follow the game plan.

25
00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:38.160
Next, let's check the bottoms. Approved

26
00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:42.100
options include black pants, black denim, blue

27
00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.660
denim, and approved Domino's joggers.

28
00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:49.140
Clothing should sit properly at the waist and be free from rips,

29
00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:53.200
tears, and distressing or anything that may look worn

30
00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:53.420
out.

31
00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:58.620
Sweatpants, leggings, basketball shorts, and other

32
00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:01.480
unapproved athletic material stays on the bench.

33
00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:05.100
And remember, shorts should be worn appropriate.

34
00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:09.259
We're delivering pizzas, not auditioning for a 1980s workout

35
00:02:09.301 --> 00:02:09.600
video.

36
00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.640
Now let's move up to the hats and hair.

37
00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:18.740
Store employees should wear a Domino's approved hat or visor

38
00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:21.080
facing forward while working.

39
00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:25.880
If your hair reaches your collar, it may need to be restrained behind your

40
00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.860
shoulders or secured appropriately.

41
00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:32.600
Depending on the job you're performing, additional hair restraints may be

42
00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:36.400
required. Your hat should say, "Ready to serve,"

43
00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:39.200
not, "I turned left and never looked back."

44
00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:42.160
Keep it forward and keep it professional.

45
00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:47.400
When preparing, handling, cutting, or boxing food,

46
00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:50.380
wear your apron properly and at full length.

47
00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:55.590
But the apron stays inside. Don't wear it outside or into

48
00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:59.360
the restroom. We want it to protect the food,

49
00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:02.100
not collecting souvenirs from everywhere you've been.

50
00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:07.360
Pins and approved accessories should also be worn only in their proper

51
00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:08.100
locations.

52
00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:12.060
Now, let's work our way down to the shoes.

53
00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:16.980
Shoes must cover the entire foot, be in good condition, and have

54
00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.910
non-slip soles. No open toes, no holes, and

55
00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:22.460
make sure your laces are tied.

56
00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:27.060
Socks are also required. Safe shoes may not be the most

57
00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:28.700
exciting part of the uniform,

58
00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:32.870
but neither is sliding across the make line like you're trying out for a night

59
00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:33.280
show.

60
00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:40.340
If you need outerwear, keep it solid black, clean,

61
00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:44.120
and in good condition with minimal outside branding.

62
00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.880
Domino's branded outerwear is also acceptable.

63
00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:52.850
Any gloves worn as part of the uniform should be black and in good

64
00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:53.380
condition.

65
00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:58.180
The goal is simple. Even when we add layers, we still look like

66
00:03:58.220 --> 00:03:59.360
one professional team.

67
00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:03.579
Perfect image goes above clothing.

68
00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:07.560
Personal cleanliness is one of the most important parts of being ready

69
00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:10.980
for work. Employees and their apparel should be clean,

70
00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:15.120
body odor should be controlled, and perfumes or lotions should be

71
00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:15.700
restrained.

72
00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:20.800
When handling food, avoid creams, oils, and lotions on your

73
00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:24.480
hands. Customers came for the smell of fresh pizza, not your

74
00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:25.900
entire bottle of cologne.

75
00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:31.140
Fingernails should be clean, neatly trimmed, and kept within

76
00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:32.200
the approved length.

77
00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:36.620
Longer nails, painted nails, or artificial nails require

78
00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:38.840
food-grade gloves while prepping food.

79
00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:43.220
This protects our products and helps maintain proper food safety

80
00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:46.960
standards. Hair must be properly secured

81
00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:50.840
under a hat or restrained away from the shoulders and food preparation

82
00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:51.300
areas.

83
00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:56.020
Facial hair is permitted, but it must be clean, neatly trimmed,

84
00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:59.820
and within the approved length. Depending on the task, a beard

85
00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:03.120
restraint may be required. Your beard can have

86
00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:04.120
personality,

87
00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:06.840
but it still has to follow the playbook.

88
00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:13.120
Keep jewelry simple and safe. Dangled earrings are not permitted,

89
00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:16.960
and facial piercings should be simple stud or a small hoop.

90
00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:21.040
Watches and bracelets should not be worn while prepping food,

91
00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:25.620
and rings used during preparation must meet the standards shown on screen.

92
00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:30.620
We want the customer focused on the pizza, not wondering whether your

93
00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:34.120
jewelry is about to become an extra topping.

94
00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:38.480
Visible tattoos must remain professional and cannot contain

95
00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:41.640
offensive images, language, nudity,

96
00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:45.020
profanity, or discriminatory references.

97
00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:49.860
Employees should also make every reasonable effort to cover

98
00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:53.660
intentional body modifications according to the appearance

99
00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:57.040
standards. Individuality is welcome.

100
00:05:57.080 --> 00:06:01.050
We just make sure what customer sees continues to represent a

101
00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:03.040
respectful workplace and brand.

102
00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:08.760
That's your perfect image game plan.

103
00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:14.560
Approved uniform, proper shoes, clean appearance, safe

104
00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:16.500
grooming, professional details.

105
00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:19.400
None of these standards work alone.

106
00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:23.260
Together, they communicate pride, preparation, and cleanliness and

107
00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:23.680
trust.

108
00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:28.960
Before every shift, take a few seconds and give yourself a quick

109
00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:32.430
pre-game check. Am I clean? Am I complete?

110
00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:36.720
Am I safe? And am I ready to represent the

111
00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:37.200
brand?

112
00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:40.760
If the answer is yes, you're game ready.

113
00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:45.900
Now that we look the part, let's learn how to play the part and create a customer

114
00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:47.860
experience worthy of Team Wow.
